# Dual-Remote Simulator

A small Java program that simulates an LG TV remote and an LG AC remote.

Requires JDK 17 or newer.

## Compile

Open a terminal inside DualRemoteSimulator and run:

```bash
javac -Xlint:unchecked -d out src/remotes/RemoteCover.java src/remotes/LGTVRemote.java src/remotes/LGACRemote.java src/Main.java
```

## Run

Run the TV example:

```bash
java -cp out Main TV
```

Run the AC example:

```bash
java -cp out Main AC
```

Run the default remote:

```bash
java -cp out Main
```

To change the default, replace `new LGTVRemote()` with
`new LGACRemote()` on the RemoteCover variable declaration in Main.java.
Then compile again and run without an argument.

## OOP concepts

- Encapsulation: each remote keeps its state and helper methods private.
- Abstraction: RemoteCover declares six abstract methods.
- Inheritance: LGTVRemote and LGACRemote extend RemoteCover.
- Polymorphism: Main uses one RemoteCover variable. The same method calls
  run different implementations depending on the selected object.

## Behaviour

The TV starts on channel 1 with a fixed volume of 20.
The channel cannot go below 1.

The AC starts at 24 C in Cooling mode.

Both devices start switched off. Counter changes work only when powered on.
Each action displays the device, power state and counter value.